* The volcano's hidden pit (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own script).
* Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder); safe to repeat.
*
* Under the volcano's lava sheet, rooms 164, 165 and 166 (x 6930-8040,
* y 2234-2399) are solid rock in the picture, but their tops were open
* doors (permeability 255) from the volcano rooms above (168, 169, 170),
* and they have no floor line of their own. A creature or object that got
* below the lava line (walking line about y 2150-2195) fell to the bottom
* of the rock, out of reach (owner, 2026-11-10). The volcano's east ledge
* (room 167) reaches down past them too, with an open door into 166.
*
* 1. Those floors are made as solid as the platforms' own floors.
setv door 0 168 164 100
setv door 0 169 165 100
setv door 0 170 166 100
setv door 0 167 166 100
*
* 2. Anything that still ends up deep in the rock (dropped there by the
* hand, say) is lifted back onto the lava line above it: a watcher
* (2 1 147, invisible) looks every 2 s for creatures and objects whose
* bottom is more than 50 px below the pit's top. The volcano's own lava
* bubbles reach only 20 px into it and are left alone. A lifted creature
* is set falling (grav 1): a walking creature keeps to the room its foot
* was in, and would at once be put back on the pit's bottom; a falling one
* lands on the floor under it, as when dropped by the hand.
enum 2 1 147 kill targ next
inst new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv cls2 2 1 147 setv attr 16 mvto 5000 1310 tick 20 slow
scrp 2 1 147 9
* inst: the whole look in one tick (without it the engine ran it 5
* instructions a tick, the timer skipped while it was still going, and it
* looked every ~17 s instead of every 2 s; measured 2026-11-12)
  inst
  enum 4 0 0
    doif posl lt 8040 doif posr gt 6930 doif posb gt 2284
      setv var0 posb subv var0 post
      setv var1 2140 subv var1 var0
      mvto posl var1
      setv grav 1
    endi endi endi
  next
  enum 2 0 0
    doif posl lt 8040 doif posr gt 6930 doif posb gt 2284
      setv var0 posb subv var0 post
      setv var1 2140 subv var1 var0
      mvto posl var1
    endi endi endi
  next
endm

* The lava flame (2 3 14, the tall flame that flares up from the floor by
* the cone machines) was at plane 0 and drew over our fruit shrubs (2 4 141,
* plane -10, food.cos) beside it when it flared (owner's screencast,
* 2026-11-13 23:47). It goes just behind them.
enum 2 3 14 plne -11 next
